<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, oil prices ease, meal steady.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, oil prices ease, meal steady.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE INDIA 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were down by 300-400 rupees per tonne on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were down on lack of demand. Soyoil solvent was down by 800 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 300 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in limited activity. Soymeal yellow was $298-300 per tonne for September-October delivery in current season.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $284-285 per tonne for November-December and January shipment in new season. Rapeseed extraction was $132-133 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,600 rupees FOR (Free on Rail) Bedibunder and was 4,550-4,575 rupees FOR (Free on Rail) Bhavnagar.</p>
